{"content": "Let me analyze the teaching examples more carefully to identify the systematic forecast errors and derivation correction rules.\n\nLooking at the examples, I need to find patterns in how the model forecasts deviate from true outcomes.\n\nLet me re-examine Example 1 more carefully:\n\nHistory (18 days): [71.56, 71.98, 73.00, 75.19, 75.94, 74.36, 74.04, 72.17, 73.46, 74.85, 76.92, 76.96, 77.98, 78.33, 79.26, 79.99, 80.27, 78.94]\n- This is the training history leading up to 2025-01-23\n- The price has been rising from ~71.56 on 2025-01-05 to ~80.27 on 2025-01-17, then back down to 78.94\n\nModel forecast (30d): [80.43, 80.91, 78.36, 79.07, 81.30, 81.12, 82.32, 79.70, 80.07, 80.64, 81.71, 82.45, 83.43, 83.63, 82.13, 80.32, 82.62, 80.96, 80.31, 79.47, 78.72, 80.53, 80.91, 79.50, 79.36, 81.82, 80.50, 81.39, 78.06, 78.60]\n\nTrue outcome (30d): [80.76, 81.67, 79.36, 80.26, 82.95, 82.66, 83.93, 80.96, 80.88, 81.12, 81.93, 82.28, 82.94, 82.59, 80.29, 78.05, 79.75, 77.21, 75.74, 74.02, 72.67, 73.90, 73.66, 71.75, 71.02, 72.78, 71.00, 71.55, 68.50,"}